   "words": 27,
   "text": "Ahkam al-Quran, 'The Commands of the Bhagavad Gita, is a 700-verse scripture Quran' an exegesis (Tafsir) of the Quran by Al-Jassas. Aisha, (612-678); daughter of Abu Bakr,"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b16",
    "p47b3"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 34,
   "text": "that is part of the Hindu epic Mahabharata. Dar us Salaam, 'Home of Peace'; referred wife of Prophet Muhammad; one of the most intellectual and influential women in Islamic history. Al-Bidaya wa'l-Nihayah, 'The Beginning"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b17"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 23,
   "text": "to as Paradise. Dawah, calling people towards God. fiqh, Islamic jurisprudence fuqaha, Islamic jurists ghulu, extremism Hunain, place in Arabia where the Battle"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b4"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 13,
   "text": "and the End' a classic work of Islamic History by scholar Ibn Kathir"
  },
  {
