   ],
   "role": "ref",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 1,
   "text": "(1301-1373)."
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b18"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 25,
   "text": "of Hunain (also Hunayn) was fought 630 AD between Prophet Muhammad and his followers and the Bedoin tribe of Hawazin. Ibn Ishaq, (704-761); historian and"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b4",
    "p47b5"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 31,
   "text": "Al-Bukhari; Imam Al-Bukhari, (810-870); Islamic scholar who authored the Hadith collection known as Sahih al-Bukhari regarded as the most authentic collection of Hadith. Al Jassas, Imam Ahmed bin Ali Abu Bakr,"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b19",
    "p47b6"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 30,
   "text": "biographer of Prophet Muhammad. Ibn Majah, (824-887); Islamic scholar and also known as al-Jassas al-Razi, died 981 AD, Islamic scholar and author Ali bin Abi Talib, died 661; cousin and"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b20",
    "p47b21"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 20,
   "text": "compiler of Hadith. Ibn Shahaab Zuhri, a traditionist or compiler of Hadith. Ikhwan, Arabic meaning—brother. Jame Al-Usool fi Ahaadith Ar-Rasool,"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
   "ids": [
    "p47b7",
    "p47b22"
   ],
   "role": "small",
   "why": "outside any article",
   "words": 28,
   "text": "son-in-law of Prophet Muhammad; the 4th Muslim Caliph. Aljame le Ahkam al-Quran, Arabic book of sayings of the Prophet by Ibnul Atheer (1209 AD). Jihad-bil-nafs, struggle against ourselves"
  },
  {
   "page": 47,
